---
import ChapterOpener from "../components/ChapterOpener.astro";
import Pager from "../components/Pager.astro";
import { formatDate, load } from "../lib/data";
import { testCounts } from "../lib/repo";

const meta = load("meta");
const status = load("status");
const bench = load("benchmark");
const golden = load("golden");
const sp = meta.splits;
const tests = testCounts();
const levels = Object.keys(golden.levels).map((a) => `${Math.round((1 - +a) * 100)}%`).join(" and ");
const checks = [
  {
    what: "Walk-forward splits",
    how: `The model is fitted on ${sp.train.start.slice(0, 4)}–${sp.train.end.slice(0, 4)}, the ranges and every sizing scale on ${sp.cal.start.slice(0, 4)}–${sp.cal.end.slice(0, 4)}. No test day informs any parameter.`,
  },
  {
    what: "Look-ahead tests",
    how: `${tests.leakage} of the ${tests.all} test functions check that features, weights, news and forecasts are unchanged when future data is altered or removed.`,
  },
  {
    what: "Delayed outcomes",
    how: `A five-day target is only known five days later, so the online methods learn each outcome ${golden.feedback_lag} trading days late, as they would live.`,
  },
  {
    what: "Python and browser agree",
    how: `The playgrounds re-implement conformal prediction in the browser. A test checks them against Python's reference values at ${levels}, to the last digit; the same goes for the lexicon reader.`,
  },
  {
    what: "Every number is generated",
    how: "Every result on this page is read from the pipeline's exported data when the site is built; none is typed in by hand.",
  },
  {
    what: "Nightly refresh",
    how: `Each weeknight GitHub Actions downloads prices, reruns the backtest and rebuilds the data. If the download fails, the last good data stays and the margin note says so. Last check: ${formatDate(status.checked.slice(0, 10))}${status.fresh === false ? ", which failed" : ""}.`,
  },
  {
    what: "Speed",
    how: `On a laptop, scoring one day takes ${bench.score_one_day.p50_ms.toFixed(2)} ms and the full walk-forward backtest of a synthetic market (${bench.test_days.toLocaleString("en-US")} test days, every method and baseline) ${bench.backtest_wall_s.toFixed(1)} s, so the method is cheap enough to run intraday.`,
  },
];
---
<section class="chapter" id="checks" aria-labelledby="checks-h">
  <ChapterOpener n="11" title="How it was checked" minutes={2} question="Could these results be flattering themselves?" hid="checks-h" />

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The easiest way to get a good backtest is to let the future leak into the past. These are the
      guards against that, and the ways you can check the work yourself.
    </p>
  </div>

  <table class="data checks">
    <caption class="visually-hidden">Checks on the study</caption>
    <tbody>
      {checks.map((c) => (
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{c.what}</th>
          <td>{c.how}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="prose reproduce">
    <p>
      For readers in model risk, the same evidence is written up as a
      <a href="https://github.com/priyanshu-mishra/aegis/blob/main/docs/MODEL_CARD.md">model validation report</a>
      in the shape a bank's review would take: the adaptive model as champion against the RiskMetrics
      incumbent, sensitivity to every setting, limitations, and the monitoring triggers that would
      call for a recalibration.
    </p>
    <p>
      To reproduce everything from a clean machine, clone
      <a href="https://github.com/priyanshu-mishra/aegis">the repository</a> and run:
    </p>
    <pre><code>pip install -e ".[dev]"
# the whole pipeline on a synthetic market, offline
python main.py demo
# real data
python main.py backtest -c configs/default.yaml
python -m pytest</code></pre>
    <p>
      Thank you for reading. I'm Priyanshu Mishra; the code is on
      <a href="https://github.com/priyanshu-mishra">GitHub</a> and I'm on
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/priyanshu-mishra-/">LinkedIn</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Pager id="checks" />
</section>

<style>
  .checks th {
    width: 11rem;
    padding-right: var(--s1);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .checks td {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  pre {
    margin: var(--s1) 0 var(--s2);
    padding: var(--s1) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .reproduce {
    margin-top: var(--s3);
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    pre {
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    .checks th {
      width: 7.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
